      <h3 class="major">A typical meeting (1:45pm to 4:30pm)</h3>
      <p>Here is what to expect when you walk in on a Saturday:</p>
      <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem; line-height:2;">
        <li><strong>1:45pm</strong> — Doors open, welcome and introductions</li>
        <li><strong>2:00pm</strong> — Meeting opens; Toastmaster of the Day sets the theme and agenda</li>
        <li><strong>2:10pm</strong> — Prepared speeches (members present pre-planned talks, typically 5 to 7 minutes each)</li>
        <li><strong>3:00pm</strong> — Short break</li>
        <li><strong>3:10pm</strong> — Table Topics (impromptu speaking — members and sometimes guests take the floor for 1 to 2 minutes on an unexpected question)</li>
        <li><strong>3:40pm</strong> — Evaluations (trained members give structured feedback on each speaker)</li>
        <li><strong>4:10pm</strong> — Reports from Timer, Ah Counter, Language Evaluator, and General Evaluator</li>
        <li><strong>4:20pm</strong> — Best Speaker, Best Table Topics, and Best Evaluator awards</li>
        <li><strong>4:30pm</strong> — Close</li>
      </ul>

